Layby Phase R, variant sync_file_range: HiCacheFile (SGLang v0.5.21, tag object 7337b27) drops its page-cache pages
as hicache_fadvise.patch does, but a write ends with sync_file_range(WAIT_BEFORE | WRITE | WAIT_AFTER) on the file's
data instead of fdatasync (no journal or metadata flush, no disk cache flush), then posix_fadvise(DONTNEED). After a
read: posix_fadvise(DONTNEED), as in the default variant. The harness picks it with the cell's
"sglang_patch_variant": "sync_file_range" when the pilot (orchestrate.py hicache-pilot) shows fdatasync throttles
HC-wt's L3 writes below stock SGLang under the cell's io.max.
Apply: engine/phase_r/sglang/apply_patch.sh PYTHON apply sync_file_range (patch -p2 in the directory that holds the
sglang package).

